# nr-tui-surface-layout: integration fragment

Fills `mixdog_tui::surface` (panel epoch, owner and claims, Enter latch and index mode, layout signature, shell layout, panel
transition, prompt rows). Nothing in it was compiled by its author (no cargo in the task); the lead compiles it with the wave.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

The `mixdog-tui` package gains one dependency edge: `mixdog-tui-widgets` (a workspace member, already in the lock). In the
`[[package]] name = "mixdog-tui"` entry, add `"mixdog-tui-widgets",` to `dependencies` (keep the list sorted). No package is
added to the lock. `mixdog-tui/Cargo.toml` already carries the edge (`mixdog-tui-widgets = { workspace = true }`, the
workspace dependency exists).

## native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

No change: the crate takes no external dependency it did not have.

## Protocol rows, SERVICE_PENDING, registrations

None. The surface is application state of the terminal UI; it registers no protocol method.

## Notes for the lead

* Tests: `cargo test --offline -p mixdog-tui` runs `surface_epoch` (the cases of shell-layout.test.mjs, panel-epoch.test.mjs and
  panel-handoff.test.mjs that need no picker factory) and `layout_twin` (golden `tests/goldens/layout.json`, 720 layouts, the
  row functions, the signature grammar, 60 sequences of surface operations). The recorder check is
  `node native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/recorders/record-layout.mjs --tree C:/Project/mixdog --check native/core/crates/mixdog-tui/tests/goldens/layout.json`
  (passed when the golden was written).
* Two helpers of the Node app live in `surface::layout` because the row budgets need them and their own tasks run in the same
  wave: `is_live_spinner_meta_visible` (live-spinner-visibility.mjs) and `btw_panel_rows` (btw-controller.mjs `btwPanelRows`).
  The tasks that port those files (nr-tui-widgets-status for the spinner, nr-tui-widgets-panels for the `/btw` panel) should call
  these instead of writing a second copy.
